.It Em recover
Reconcile runs that were interrupted, so they can be undone.
.Pp
A run that was killed or lost power before it finished is listed as interrupted, and `dtidy run` refuses to start until it is reconciled. Recover checks every planned move of each interrupted run by file identity, records whether the file is at its source or its destination, and marks the run as recovered. A recovered run can then be undone like any other run.

EXAMPLES:
  dtidy recover
      Reconcile every interrupted run.
  dtidy recover && dtidy undo
      Reconcile, then put the files of the most recent run back.
