.It Em config
Manage the configuration file.
.Pp
dtidy works without a config file. A config file sets the root folder, the bucket rules and what is skipped, and it replaces the built-in rules rather than adding to them, so start from `dtidy config init`. The file is read from --config, otherwise $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dtidy/config.json, otherwise ~/.config/dtidy/config.json.

EXAMPLES:
  dtidy config init
      Write the built-in defaults as a starting point.
  dtidy config path
      Show which config file is in effect.
  dtidy config validate
      Check the config file without touching the Desktop.
